  "raw_output": "{\n  \"exercise_type\": \"CEFR English Placement Test\",\n  \"section_id\": 5,\n  \"section_title\": \"Reading Comprehension\",\n  \"cefr_range\": \"B2-C1\",\n  \"reading_text\": \"The concept of 'glocalization' was first introduced by Mark Gottdiener in the 1990s. It refers to the process of adapting global products and services to meet local tastes and preferences. This phenomenon is particularly evident in the food industry, where multinational corporations such as McDonald's and Starbucks have modified their menus to suit regional markets.\n\nFor example, in Japan, McDonald's offers a Teriyaki McBurger, while in India, they provide a McAloo Tikki, which consists of a potato and pea patty. Similarly, Starbucks has introduced a range of local flavors, including green tea and matcha lattes, to cater to the Japanese market.\n\nGlocalization is not without its critics, however. Some argue that it leads to cultural homogenization, where local cultures are lost in favor of globalized products. Others claim that glocalization is simply a marketing strategy to increase profits.\n\nDespite these concerns, glocalization has become an essential aspect of modern business. Companies must adapt to changing consumer preferences and tastes, or risk losing market share. As the world becomes increasingly interconnected, the need for glocalization will only continue to grow.\",\n  \"questions\": [\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 36,\n      \"question\": \"What is the main idea of the article about?\",\n      \"options\": [\"The benefits of globalization\", \"The concept of glocalization and its effects on local cultures\", \"The rise of multinational corporations in the food industry\", \"The impact of social media on consumer behavior\"],\n      \"answer\": \"The concept of glocalization and its effects on local cultures\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 37,\n      \"question\": \"According to the article, what is an example of a product that McDonald's offers in Japan?\",\n      \"options\": [\"McAloo Tikki\", \"Teriyaki McBurger\", \"Big Mac\", \"Quarter Pounder with Cheese\"],\n      \"answer\": \"Teriyaki McBurger\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 38,\n      \"question\": \"What is the author's attitude towards glocalization?\",\n      \"options\": [\"Neutral\", \"Positive\", \"Negative\", \"Ambivalent\"],\n      \"answer\": \"Neutral\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 39,\n      \"question\": \"Why do companies engage in glocalization, according to the article?\",\n      \"options\": [\"To increase profits\", \"To reduce costs\", \"To adapt to changing consumer preferences and tastes\", \"To expand their market share\"],\n      \"answer\": \"To adapt to changing consumer preferences and tastes\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 40,\n      \"question\": \"What is a potential drawback of glocalization, according to the article?\",\n      \"options\": [\"Cultural homogenization\", \"Increased competition from local businesses\", \"Higher production costs\", \"Decreased consumer satisfaction\"],\n      \"answer\": \"Cultural homogenization\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
